{
 "file": "exact-amount.json",
 "description": "The exact amount rule (money stage 1). imd-flop: amount.ts exactAmount(value). viewer: build-lane.py exact(value). An exact amount is a string of ASCII decimal digits only whose value is below 2^128 (rules.json EXACT_AMOUNT_BOUND), returned in canonical form: no leading zeros, \"0\" for zero. Anything else is unknown (null), never 0. Per FLOP's own sources, read 2026-11-11: the chain counts money in whole base units, 10^18 per FLOP, in a u128, and the gateway receipt (OpenAPI CredentialReceipt) carries settled_spend_raw as a string matching ^[0-9]+$ in base units, or null. A vector whose input has no value key stands for a missing field.",
 "status": "money stage 1",
